{"model": "gpt-oss-120b", "input": [{"role": "developer", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "Assess the full current SHACL using these distinct inputs:\n- Regulation establishes the represented obligation.\n- Declared schema/mappings establish RDF identifiers, ownership, paths, datatypes and units; a similar label is not an equivalent mapping.\n- Approved scope establishes declared external research assumptions, not real-vessel certification. Conditions inside the represented requirement remain in scope.\n- Candidate code is what you assess, not source/schema evidence.\n- Execution diagnostics establish observed technical behavior, not regulatory correctness or full coverage.\n\nProcedure:\n1. Read the represented requirement and approved scope.\n2. Compare its conditions and obligations with the full current code, including activation, query branches and supplied changes/removals.\n3. Report supported code defects as issues with actionable corrections. Preserve unaffected obligations; do not propose deletion just to pass checks.\n4. Report genuinely missing or contradictory information as context questions, without inventing a code defect.\n5. Explicitly address every carried-forward question using question_review; use current supplied evidence to support resolution/withdrawal. STILL_UNRESOLVED remains blocking.\n6. Return one complete JSON object matching expected_response_schema and its authoritative description. Make assessment consistent with issues, questions, carried-forward questions and change/gap assessments. Delivery is separate from approval.\n\nEvidence references identify supplied E entries only. Generic evidence-field example: \"evidence\":[\"E7\"] (valid only if E7 is supplied). Optional evidence character spans refer to that entry, not code; asserted quotations must match exactly. RDF_FACT references cite the whole atomic fact.\nCode locations belong in issues[].location. Generic location-field example: \"location\":{\"start\":1,\"end\":1,\"unit\":\"lines\"} (valid only if current line 1 exists). Software extracts exact code and binds hashes; do not quote code or invent an evidence ID such as candidate_shape. Missing constraints use a real insertion anchor. Context questions/dispositions need no code location.\n\nCitations support claims, not their interpretation. Regulation need not contain RDF IRIs; mappings do not establish formulas or compliance answers. Keep missing mappings unresolved. Proposed representation changes must pair each operand's declared property/path/role; unit renaming is not conversion. Review supplied prior issues and functional changes/removals, including reachable replacements, using the documented conditional fields. Software owns IDs and bookkeeping.\n\nFailed responses authorize no repair and create no accepted issues. For a response correction, keep the same candidate, evidence and original prior state; return the complete corrected review. Never request evaluation fixtures, labels, counterparts or historical solutions.\n"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "{\"candidate_version\": 2, \"candidate_sha256\": \"44da656fa9a9e182771be2656545dbf490f21c3f11c98d7762ec7baa2c27014e\", \"review_request_id\": \"review:8db5a2e2d65ed074bd44b3944054be64c1611fb23dde7ea18d4c14b74c52fb9c\", \"full_candidate\": \"@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\\n@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\\n@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/shacl#> .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Shape that captures the welding requirement for weld entities.\\n# It is **not** a target shape; it is only invoked from the ship shape\\n# via the hasWeld property (see ex:ShipShape below).  This respects the\\n# admission boundary which declares the population owner class as\\n# https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship.\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nex:WeldRequirementShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    ## Requirement: if a weld is within an ice‑strengthened area,\\n    ## then its weld type must be the double continuous weld.\\n    ## Expressed as: ( NOT withinIceStrengthenedArea ) OR ( weldType = doubleContinuousWeld )\\n    sh:or (\\n        # Case 1 – the weld is **not** within an ice‑strengthened area.\\n        [\\n            sh:property [\\n                sh:path vocab:withinIceStrengthenedArea ;\\n                sh:hasValue false ;\\n                sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;\\n                sh:message \\\"Weld is not within an ice‑strengthened area.\\\" ;\\n            ] ;\\n        ]\\n        # Case 2 – the weld is within an ice‑strengthened area and must be double‑continuous.\\n        [\\n            sh:property [\\n                sh:path vocab:weldType ;\\n                sh:hasValue vocab:doubleContinuousWeld ;\\n                sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;\\n                sh:message \\\"Weld within ice‑strengthened area must be of type double continuous.\\\" ;\\n            ] ;\\n        ]\\n    ) ;\\n    sh:message \\\"Weld does not satisfy the double‑continuous requirement for ice‑strengthened areas.\\\" .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Ship shape that links ships to their welds and enforces the weld\\n# requirement on each associated weld.\\n# The target class is exactly the declared owner class, satisfying the\\n# admission scope constraint.\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nex:ShipShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path vocab:hasWeld ;\\n        sh:node ex:WeldRequirementShape ;\\n        sh:message \\\"Associated weld must satisfy the double‑continuous requirement when positioned in ice‑strengthened areas.\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    sh:message \\\"Ship has welds that violate the double‑continuous welding rule for ice‑strengthened areas.\\\" .\\n\", \"previous_candidate\": {\"version\": 1, \"sha256\": \"3042f1604b1e45f826b4426b2cf504a6143f9259fdbddbd87834d7880a874f41\", \"full_code\": \"@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\\n@prefix ex: <http://example.org/shacl#> .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Shape that captures the welding requirement for weld entities.\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nex:WeldRequirementShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass vocab:weld ;\\n    ## Requirement: if a weld is within an ice‑strengthened area,\\n    ## then its weld type must be the double continuous weld.\\n    ## Expressed as: ( NOT withinIceStrengthenedArea ) OR ( weldType = doubleContinuousWeld )\\n    sh:or (\\n        # Case 1 – the weld is **not** within an ice‑strengthened area.\\n        [\\n            sh:property [\\n                sh:path vocab:withinIceStrengthenedArea ;\\n                sh:hasValue false ;\\n                sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;\\n                sh:message \\\"Weld is not within an ice‑strengthened area.\\\" ;\\n            ] ;\\n        ]\\n        # Case 2 – the weld is within an ice‑strengthened area and must be double‑continuous.\\n        [\\n            sh:property [\\n                sh:path vocab:weldType ;\\n                sh:hasValue vocab:doubleContinuousWeld ;\\n                sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;\\n                sh:message \\\"Weld within ice‑strengthened area must be of type double continuous.\\\" ;\\n            ] ;\\n        ]\\n    ) ;\\n    sh:message \\\"Weld does not satisfy the double‑continuous requirement for ice‑strengthened areas.\\\" .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Ship shape that links ships to their welds and enforces the weld\\n# requirement on each associated weld.\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nex:ShipShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path vocab:hasWeld ;\\n        sh:node ex:WeldRequirementShape ;\\n        sh:message \\\"Associated weld must satisfy the double‑continuous requirement when positioned in ice‑strengthened areas.\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    sh:message \\\"Ship has welds that violate the double‑continuous welding rule for ice‑strengthened areas.\\\" .\\n\"}, \"max_issues\": 12, \"expected_response_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"assessment\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"APPROVE\", \"HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED\", \"REJECT\"]}, \"issues\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"quote\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"id\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}]}, \"minItems\": 1, \"maxItems\": 8}, \"location\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"lines\", \"characters\"]}}, \"required\": [\"start\", \"end\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"suggestion\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"operands\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"property\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"path\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"minItems\": 1}, \"role\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"PROPERTY\", \"NUMERIC_OPERAND\"]}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"datatype\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"property\", \"path\", \"role\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"minItems\": 1, \"maxItems\": 8}}, \"required\": [\"description\", \"evidence\", \"location\", \"suggestion\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"maxItems\": 12}, \"questions\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"missing\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"why\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"kind\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"source\", \"schema\"]}, \"reference\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"maxLength\": 100}, \"section\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"quote\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"id\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}]}, \"maxItems\": 8}}, \"required\": [\"missing\", \"why\", \"kind\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"maxItems\": 3}, \"change_review\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"enum\": [\"C1\"]}, \"disposition\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"SUPPORTED\", \"REGRESSION\", \"UNRESOLVED\"]}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"evidence\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"quote\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"id\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}]}, \"minItems\": 1, \"maxItems\": 8}, \"issue\": {\"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"disposition\", \"reason\", \"evidence\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"minItems\": 1, \"maxItems\": 1}, \"gap_review\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"enum\": [\"G1\", \"G2\", \"G3\", \"G4\", \"G5\"]}, \"material\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"why\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"material\", \"why\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"maxItems\": 5}}, \"required\": [\"assessment\", \"issues\", \"questions\", \"change_review\", \"gap_review\"], \"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Return complete assessment, issues and questions. APPROVE requires no current/prior issue or material question, all changes SUPPORTED and every supplied gap explicitly nonmaterial. REJECT needs an actionable code issue. HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED needs a new/carried-forward material question or unresolved change/gap. Issue fields: description, evidence, location, suggestion. Evidence uses supplied E IDs or {id,start?,end?,quote?}; paired start/end are character offsets in that evidence, not code. RDF_FACT citations use the whole fact. Optional quotes are checked exactly. location uses start/end and optional unit=lines (default) or characters, on the full current candidate; software extracts exact code. Context questions/dispositions have no location and need no invented defect. Assess each supplied C ID once. REGRESSION links an actionable zero-based issue index; UNRESOLVED blocks approval. For APPROVE assess each G ID with material=false and why; material gaps require questions. Software owns hashes, IDs and reconciliation. Review supplied prior issues without returning duplicate bookkeeping. Unsupported assertions, invented references/quotes and inconsistent decisions are invalid; citation interpretation remains model judgment.\"}, \"execution_probe\": {\"candidate_version\": 2, \"candidate_sha256\": \"44da656fa9a9e182771be2656545dbf490f21c3f11c98d7762ec7baa2c27014e\", \"engine\": \"pyshacl\", \"engine_version\": \"0.31.0\", \"engine_outcome\": \"COMPLETED_NO_ENGINE_ERROR\", \"diagnostic_availability\": \"Captured verbatim\", \"activation\": {\"roots\": [\"http://example.org/shacl#ShipShape\"], \"reachable\": [\"http://example.org/shacl#ShipShape\", \"http://example.org/shacl#WeldRequirementShape\", \"n227cd5f38fe945b5b6ee24c39b62067bb1\", \"n227cd5f38fe945b5b6ee24c39b62067bb2\", \"n227cd5f38fe945b5b6ee24c39b62067bb3\", \"n227cd5f38fe945b5b6ee24c39b62067bb4\", \"n227cd5f38fe945b5b6ee24c39b62067bb7\"], \"enforcing_nodes\": [\"n227cd5f38fe945b5b6ee24c39b62067bb2\", \"n227cd5f38fe945b5b6ee24c39b62067bb4\"], \"deactivated_reachable\": [], \"orphan_constraint_nodes\": [], \"unsupported_custom_targets\": [], \"supported\": true}, \"regulatory_correctness_established\": false, \"scope\": \"Execution-only schema-derived probe; no expected regulatory verdict; success is not complete correctness\", \"diagnostics\": {\"stdout\": {\"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\", \"characters\": 0, \"artifact_field\": \"execution_probe.exact_diagnostics.stdout\"}, \"stderr\": {\"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\", \"characters\": 0, \"artifact_field\": \"execution_probe.exact_diagnostics.stderr\"}}}, \"citation_format\": {\"evidence\": \"E ID, optional character span. Server resolves exact text/hash/provenance. quote optional and checked if asserted.\", \"code\": \"location {start,end,unit?}; default one-based inclusive lines, optional characters half-open. Server binds version/hash.\", \"roles\": \"SOURCE: obligation. SCHEMA_TEXT/RDF_FACT: representation. CALLER_DECLARATION: external research population. No legal IRI requirement; no formulas inferred from mappings.\"}, \"protocol_version\": 2, \"context\": {\"requirement\": {\"id\": \"I2-066\", \"source\": \"UR I2 Structural Requirements for Polar Class Ships\", \"clause\": \"I2.18.1\"}, \"scope\": \"Implement and review the supplied source in the declared schema. No supplied compliance solution or expected verdict. Material unspecified representation/applicability prevents acceptance. External population/date eligibility and edition selection are supplied by caller admission, not independently inferred from RDF. Conditions within the represented requirement remain in scope; activation and query correctness are separate obligations.\", \"source_selection\": {\"manifest_sha256\": \"90c004983238a9b5fdd2d3a2911a064c8186bb8592de1a5dc8ffbc8b839328bb\", \"included_characters\": 2580, \"original_characters\": 62501, \"omitted_sections\": 106, \"retrieval\": \"Schema.source_evidence(file, document_sha256, start, end); complete sections/hashes retained in source_selection_manifest.json; missing necessary evidence must remain unresolved\"}, \"source_completeness\": \"Deterministic source selection, not a proof of complete context. Ambiguous primary anchors retain full source; unresolved references require review.\"}, \"admission_sha256\": \"385b2eb55b74ccb9220ef3c7046a9fbfdf59a9e658318381de45699464291385\", \"evidence_catalog\": {\"format_version\": 2, \"catalog_sha256\": \"8455e15785f923a9c51c2cd5662d1393f90da78d87e64b08bf8a5583abb5431e\", \"entries\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"E1\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#weldTypeValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E2\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designOperationSpeedInIce> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Quantity metadata requires the canonical QUDT QuantityValue node pattern\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E3\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#navigatingInIce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Navigating in ice\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E4\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceLoadSourceType> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Applicable TRAFICOM regulation wording plus explicit engineering node/operand role\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E5\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#weld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Weld\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E6\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#otherIceStrengthenedArea> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-R10-0081\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E7\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#supportsIceStrengthenedFrames> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Typed literal required for applicability, state, identification, or non-quantity evidence.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E8\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#weldTypeValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Weld type value\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E9\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceTypeValue> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-R9-0180\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E10\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipOperatesInIceCoveredWaters> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-068\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E11\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designOperationSpeedInIce> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"designOperationSpeedInIce\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E12\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#weldTypeValue\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"Class\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Weld type value\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"weldTypeValue\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-050 | TRAFICOM p.21 | 4.4.4.2; I2-066 | IACS_UR_I2 p.22 | I2.18.1\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E13\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#markingPlainlyVisibleInIceConditions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Marking plainly visible in ice conditions\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E14\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#operatingIceType> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Locked-workbook normalized regulatory term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E15\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#weld> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"I2-066\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E16\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#internalIceStrengthenedStructure> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (R9 development): Internal ice strengthened structure represents the linked requirement entity, relationship, value, evidence role, or quantity; its scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E17\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#internalIceStrengthenedStructure> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-R9-0186\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E18\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#doubleContinuousWeld> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Applicable TRAFICOM regulation wording plus explicit engineering node/operand role\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E19\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#navigatingInIce> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-B01-169\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E20\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"                                                                                                           I2\\n\\n\\n\\nI2          Structural Requirements for Polar Class Ships\\n(August\\n(cont)\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IACS_I2_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 0, \"end\": 186}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E21\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceReference> \\\"IMO26-002 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.2 | Chapter 9-1 applicability; IMO26-016 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.5 | Chapter 11-1 applicability\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E22\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceTypeValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E23\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceLoadSourceTypeValue> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-057\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E24\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#locatedWithinIceBelt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Batch 01 development): Located within ice belt is the benchmark representation of the linked requirement operand, relationship, evidence role, or controlled value. Exact scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E25\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designOperationSpeedInIce> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Verified recommended QUDT unit from Stage 1 or a documented Stage 2 source-unit refinement\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E26\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipOperatesInIceCoveredWaters> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E27\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designOperationSpeedInIce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E28\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \