\"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E408\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"xsd:boolean\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#navigatingInIce\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"DatatypeProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Navigating in ice\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"navigatingInIce\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-015 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-016 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E409\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sidescuttleInIceBelt> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E410\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#navigatingInIce> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Batch 01 development): Navigating in ice is the benchmark representation of the linked requirement operand, relationship, evidence role, or controlled value. Exact scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E411\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipOperatesInIceCoveredWaters> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#module> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleCore> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E412\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#otherIceStrengthenedAreaValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (R9 development): Other ice strengthened area value represents the linked requirement entity, relationship, value, evidence role, or quantity; its scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E413\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Cargo ship\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E414\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#markingPlainlyVisibleInIceConditions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Marking plainly visible in ice conditions\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E415\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#continuousPropulsionPowerAvailableInIce> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Development unit selected and fixture conversion required\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E416\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#oilTanker\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"Class\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Oil tanker\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"oilTanker\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"IMO-109 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.41 | 1.2.2; IMO-110 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.41 | 1.2.3\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E417\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipIceStrengthened> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceAlias> \\\"ship_ice_strengthened\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E418\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sidescuttleInIceBelt> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"In addition, the following areas shall be strengthened: Fore foot: For ice class IA Super, the shell plating below the ice belt from the stem to a position five main frame spacings abaft of the point where the bow profile departs from the keel line shall be ice-strengthened in the same way as the bow region. Upper bow ice belt: For ice classes IA Super and I...\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E419\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipIceStrengthened> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E420\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hullRegionValue> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-B01-106\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E421\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hullAreaValue> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-R10-0055\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E422\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E423\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipOperatesInIceCoveredWaters> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for shipOperatesInIceCoveredWaters derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E424\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\